            <div xml:id="d1164">

                <pb facs="1051" n="737" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg737"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 704.6361/5a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé d’Affaires in
                        Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-09T20:00:00-05:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 9, 1914, 8 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Your August 8, 10 a.m. Department approves your course in protesting against any
                    molestation of embassies temporarily in our charge, but if after protest the
                    Government insists upon taking automobiles, the matter will be dealt with by
                    diplomatic correspondence. You should not use force to prevent an execution of
                    the Government’s orders if it decides to remove automobiles.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
